I am applying for the Senior Software Engineer, AI Builder Experience role at=
 MongoDB.

At Black Piano, I build production agentic workflows and tool interfaces in P=
ython. My work includes developing a custom MCP tool that generates data-grou=
nded content from structured pipelines, as well as an autonomous self-healing=
 data-quality agent powered by Gemini with automated fallback, retries, and e=
scalation gates. Independently, I built and published MyLocalCLI on npm, a te=
rminal coding assistant featuring a Stdio MCP bridge, parallel tool dispatch,=
 automatic provider failover across eight backends, and forty-two built-in en=
gineering tools.

My other independent projects center on robust multi-agent orchestration and =
bounded autonomy. I developed JobAgents in Python, orchestrating agent pipeli=
nes across multiple CLI harnesses to extract and deterministically match job =
postings with zero unnecessary LLM calls. In BugAgents and AgentSwarm, I engi=
neered per-turn tool-call auditing, workspace-corroborated promotion gates, a=
nd tamper-proof hash-chained ledgers that verify multi-agent outputs, benchma=
rk execution across diverse substrates, and prevent phantom actions.

MongoDB provides the critical data foundation for modern intelligent software=
, and I want to help create the developer abstractions, MCP interfaces, and a=
gentic frameworks that empower builders worldwide.

I welcome the opportunity to discuss how my hands-on background in Python, MC=
P integration, and agent orchestration can contribute to the AI Builder Exper=
ience team.

Prashanth Kumar Kadasi
